# T3 LIVE LED states: off (empty), dim (loaded), on (playing), fast blink (queued to start)
# and slow blink (queued to stop). The levels are the single-colour ones X0X offers: lit and
# dim; "blinking" is the UI toggling between them each frame.
wait 300
# T7a: enter the classic X0X pages (GLOBAL -> Classic patterns).
tap GLO
tap SEL
# two 909 patterns, so there is a second drum clip to queue
tapkey w0
turn PRESET 1
tapkey w2
turn PRESET -1
# enter LIVE
# T7a: the song is the edited object; seed its clips from the patterns just built.
songseed
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 50
expect mode 1
# empty (key 2) and loaded (key 0, a clip not playing)
expect key 2 0
expect key 0 1
# playing: launch drum A and start the transport
tapkey 0
tap PLAY
wait-bar 1
expect key 0 2
# queued to start: queue drum B on a fresh bar; its key blinks
wait-bar 1
tapkey 1
keyblink b0
# cancel it: the key is loaded (dim) again
tapkey 1
expect key 1 1
# queued to stop: tap the playing clip; its key slow-blinks
wait-bar 1
tapkey 0
keyblink w0 slow
shot live_leds.png
dump live_leds.json
# leave LIVE
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
expect mode 0
